    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>When the Catholic Church dissolved the Jesuit order, missionary Marc Arsenault was left isolated in a native settlement in the Ottawa Valley; en route back to Montreal he was attacked and Embraced by a nomadic pack of Country Gangrel, and, drawn by his correspondence with Soeur Jeanne, joined the Shepherds of Caine. Marc never abandoned his drive to understand and convert the Quebec natives, and became fascinated by tales of natives who never survive the Embrace &mdash; he has Embraced hundreds over the centuries in cursed ground on Mount Royal, and none have survived more than a night. Convinced a demonic force on the mountain is responsible, he has spent a century investigating, torturing the enigmatic Tremere antitribu Jacob the Glitch and flaying native victims to understand their deaths, even &quot;borrowing&quot; the preserved heart of the mortal saint Frère André for his own rituals. He led the Shepherds from 1951 until Sangris' fall was blamed in part on his obsession, and now leaves coven affairs to Yitzhak and Alfred Benezri.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>Focused on your goals. The mysteries of Mount Royal and the native nations cannot elude you forever; you will do anything to pierce the veil.</p><h2>Secrets</h2><p>Frère Marc understands more about Mount Royal's demon than almost anyone: that it is a fiend of disease with access to feral creatures, and that it may not have been destroyed along with Sangris.</p>",
    "notes": "Embraced 1799. Apparent age: late 30s. Path of Nocturnal Redemption 7. Disciplines (as printed): Auspex 4, Animalism 3, Fortitude 3, Protean 4, Thaumaturgy 4 (Corruption 3, Spirit Thaumaturgy 4, Gift of Morpheus 3).",
    "npcType": "vampire"
  },
